# Auto deploy after development (always)

When **development on the live line** (`app_15.0/`) is **finished and verified** in this session, **always** auto-deploy to shinyapps.io. Do **not** wait for the user to say「部署」or「推送」.

Immediately run the full ship sequence from the **coding clone** (`/Users/lawrencekuo/coding/theYNowApp`):

1. **Version bump (+0.01):** update display version strings per `.cursor/rules/version-bump-on-merge.mdc` (until user switches to +1).
2. **Commit** only the relevant app changes (message: why, 1–2 sentences).  
   - This repo’s Git may reject `git commit --trailer`; if so use `write-tree` → `commit-tree` → `update-ref`.
3. **`git push origin HEAD`**
4. **Deploy:** `Rscript scripts/deploy_app_15.R`  
   - Confirm live bundle via rsconnect (`status=running`, new `bundleId`).  
   - If local client dies (disk) but upload succeeded, poll until the new bundle is active before recording baseline.
5. **Baseline:** update `scripts/DEPLOY_BASELINE.txt` (bundleId, aligned_git/commit/short, message, `captured_at`, display version if noted), commit as `chore: record shinyapps baseline bundle <id> (app_15.0)`, push.
6. Briefly report: app commit, baseline commit, display version, bundleId, live URL.

## Applies when (default = ship)

- Any completed feature, fix, UI/logic change, optimization, or other **app behavior** work on `app_15.0/` that is verified in-session.
- Explicit「部署／推送」is **not** required once development is complete.

## Does **not** apply (ask or skip ship)

- Exploratory Q&A, plans, or incomplete / broken work
- Docs-only / chore-only / rules-only with **no** app behavior change (unless user asks to deploy)
- User says not to deploy, or only wants a local/WIP commit
- Secrets, `.Renviron`, or unrelated paths outside the agreed ship set

Prefer coding-clone git ops; do not run git inside the OneDrive mirror. OneDrive sync is best-effort and may hang—do not block ship on it.
